saral is a terminal client for Jira Cloud.

usage:
  saral [flags] [view | issue key | Jira URL]
  saral <command> [flags]

views:
  list      Issues    g 1
  board     Board     g 2
  backlog   Backlog   g 3
  sprints   Sprints   g 4
  releases  Releases  g 5
  timeline  Timeline  g 6
  plans     Plans     g 7
  settings  Settings  

commands:
  doctor   check the config, the token, the site and the cache; the output is safe to paste
  help     print this help
  version  print the version, where the config lives, and what the terminal reports

examples:
  saral                       open where you left off, or setup on a first run
  saral board --project PROJ  the board, scoped to one project
  saral PROJ-142              one issue; a pasted Jira URL works too

inside:
  ?       every key the view in front of you takes
  ctrl+k  the command palette: every action, view and issue on disk

flags:
  --fake               demo mode: synthetic issues in memory, no site, no token, nothing saved
  --glyphs   string    unicode, nerd or ascii; unicode is the default, nerd needs a Nerd Font
  --log      string    write a debug log to this file; tokens and emails are redacted
  --mouse              enable mouse reporting
  --poll     duration  re-read the focused view every duration, e.g. 30s; off by default, and pauses when Jira rate-limits
  --profile  string    profile to use (default: $SARAL_PROFILE, then the active one)
  --project  string    project key to scope the session to; several capabilities are per-project
  --scheme   string    default, nord, dracula, solarized or gruvbox
  --theme    string    auto, dark, light or no-color
  --version            print the version and exit

files:
  config  $SARAL_CONFIG_DIR/config.toml
  cache   $SARAL_CACHE_DIR/cache.db

environment:
  SARAL_CONFIG_DIR         where config.toml lives
  SARAL_CACHE_DIR          where the cache lives
  SARAL_PROFILE            the profile to use when --profile is not given
  SARAL_SITE, SARAL_EMAIL  override the profile's site and email, or stand in for a config file
  SARAL_TOKEN              the API token; read from the environment only, never written to the file
  HTTPS_PROXY, NO_PROXY    the proxy requests go through
  NO_COLOR                 turn colour off whatever the theme says
  precedence: flags, then the environment, then config.toml

exit codes:
  0  success
  1  anything else: the site could not be reached, a request failed
  2  a flag or argument was not understood
  3  config.toml or the profile is unusable
  4  the token could not be found, or the site refused it
